<!--
  NEGATIVE FIXTURE. Do not "fix" the TransferCharacteristics value below.

  This profile carries a HAGC tone-mapping descriptor (clause 8.10.3 a), so it
  is asserting the HDR Profile mechanism of clause 8.10. Its cicpTag then
  declares TransferCharacteristics 13 (IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB), which clause 8.10.1
  forbids: "Other values of TransferCharacteristics shall not be used in an HDR
  Profile", the permitted set being 8 (Linear), 16 (PQ) and 18 (HLG).

  This is the case that makes the clause's definition non-circular. An HDR
  Profile is defined as carrying a cicpTag with one of those three values, so a
  profile that gets the field wrong is, read literally, simply not an HDR
  Profile and violates nothing. The HAGC tag is the independent evidence of HDR
  intent that lets a validator say the value is wrong rather than say nothing.

  Expected: iccFromXml saves the profile, and iccDumpProfile -v reports
    "HDR: cicp TransferCharacteristics is 13"
  See Testing/expected-invalid-fromxml.tsv.
-->
